  "title": "Advance releases configuration admission before ApplyConfChange",
  "cause": "Configuration admission compares pendingConfIndex against raftLog.applied, which Advance can move before the separate membership-application callback.",
  "trigger": "The caller advances released configuration work before applying that membership change and submits subsequent configuration work; see the retained original confirmation.",
  "consequence": "A later configuration change can commit before the preceding configuration has taken effect, violating the recorded one-change-at-a-time boundary.",
  "sites": [
    "raft.go:stepLeader",
    "raft.go:advance",
    "node.go:run",
    "node.go:Advance",
    "node.go:ApplyConfChange"
  ],
  "actions": [],
  "invariants": [],
  "premises": [
    "This is inherited completed V01 public Node confirmation, not a fresh reproduction in the calibration or a later update.",
    "The supported caller contract permits Advance before the distinct ApplyConfChange callback and does not externally serialize all subsequent configuration proposals until application.",
    "The admission cursor, wrapper handoff, and observable configuration-commit consequence retain their recorded meanings; changes to those premises or dependencies require targeted reanalysis.",
    "The reusable conclusion is source-level and backed by the archived native confirmation; no TLA+ model operator is part of that reproduction's execution."
